<title>USA: S.Africa to accept some US wheat from fungus areas.</title>
<headline>S.Africa to accept some US wheat from fungus areas.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa has agreed to accept U.S. wheat from karnal bunt quarantine areas if it has twice tested negative for the fungus, Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman announced Tuesday.</p>
<p>Glickman, who just returned from South Africa where he met with South African agriculture minister Derek Hanekom on the issue, said the agreement is worth about $34 million to U.S. wheat farmers.</p>
</text>
